From: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Subject: [PATCH] net/sched: sch_cake: give the shaper timer slack

When the shaper holds the next packet back, CAKE arms its watchdog for
the exact time that packet may leave. At a few hundred Mbit/s that is a
timer interrupt, a softirq and a qdisc run for nearly every packet: on a
4x Cortex-A53 router shaping 310 Mbit/s of download, the queue stopped
on the shaper 1.29 times per packet sent.

Let the timer fire up to four packet times late, capped at 100 us, as
sch_fq does with its timer_slack. The shaper keeps its rate, since it
sends what it owes once the timer runs. On the same router the shaper
stops fell to 0.48 per packet and the CPU time per GB forwarded from
14369 to 10481 ms (100 us slack, 8 flows, 4 runs each), at the same
throughput. Four packet times are 156 us at 310 Mbit/s, where the cap
applies, 48 us at 1 Gbit/s and 5 us at 10 Gbit/s.

Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
---
--- a/net/sched/sch_cake.c
+++ b/net/sched/sch_cake.c
@@ -232,6 +232,7 @@ struct cake_sched_data {
 	/* time_next = time_this + ((len * rate_ns) >> rate_shft) */
 	ktime_t		time_next_packet;
 	ktime_t		failsafe_next_packet;
+	u64		timer_slack;
 	u64		rate_ns;
 	u16		rate_shft;
 	u16		overflow_timeout;
@@ -1795,7 +1796,8 @@ static s32 cake_enqueue(struct sk_buff *
 					    ktime_to_ns(
 						   q->failsafe_next_packet));
 				sch->qstats.overlimits++;
-				qdisc_watchdog_schedule_ns(&q->watchdog, next);
+				qdisc_watchdog_schedule_range_ns(&q->watchdog, next,
+								 q->timer_slack);
 			}
 		}
 	}
@@ -2062,7 +2064,8 @@ begin:
 			       ktime_to_ns(q->failsafe_next_packet));
 
 		sch->qstats.overlimits++;
-		qdisc_watchdog_schedule_ns(&q->watchdog, next);
+		qdisc_watchdog_schedule_range_ns(&q->watchdog, next,
+						 q->timer_slack);
 		return NULL;
 	}
 
@@ -2302,7 +2305,8 @@ retry:
 		u64 next = min(ktime_to_ns(q->time_next_packet),
 			       ktime_to_ns(q->failsafe_next_packet));
 
-		qdisc_watchdog_schedule_ns(&q->watchdog, next);
+		qdisc_watchdog_schedule_range_ns(&q->watchdog, next,
+						 q->timer_slack);
 	} else if (!sch->q.qlen) {
 		int i;
 
@@ -2651,6 +2655,16 @@ static void cake_configure_rates(struct
 
 	qd->rate_ns   = qd->tins[ft].tin_rate_ns;
 	qd->rate_shft = qd->tins[ft].tin_rate_shft;
+
+	/* Waking the shaper for every packet costs a timer interrupt and a
+	 * softirq each. Letting the timer fire up to four packet times late
+	 * lets it send a few at once, as sch_fq's timer_slack does; the shaper
+	 * still meets its rate, since it catches up on what it owes. Capped so
+	 * that a slow link waits no longer than a fast one would.
+	 */
+	qd->timer_slack = min_t(u64, 100 * NSEC_PER_USEC,
+				(4ULL * psched_mtu(qdisc_dev(sch)) * qd->rate_ns) >>
+				qd->rate_shft);
 }
 
 static void cake_reconfigure(struct Qdisc *sch)
